+Layout of the data at the integration points
+--------------------------------------------
+
+The arrays of the data at the integration points of a material (gradients,
+thermodynamic forces, internal state variables and energies at the
+beginning and at the end of the time step, tangent operator blocks) are
+stored in one of the two layouts of :code:`MGIS` (:code:`mgis::FieldLayout`):
+
+- :code:`PointByPoint` (default): the components of a point are
+  contiguous;
+- :code:`ComponentByComponent`: the values of a component are contiguous,
+  which gives coalesced accesses on a GPU to the kernels using one thread
+  per point, such as the integration of the behaviours generated by the
+  :code:`generic-parallel` interface.
+
+The parameter :code:`QuadratureDataLayout` of the problem gives the layout
+of all its materials. The parameter of the same name of
+:code:`addBehaviourIntegrator` replaces it for one material, so that the
+materials of a problem may use different layouts, for instance when some
+are integrated on the host and others on a GPU. The point-wise models
+(:code:`PointWiseModel`) accept the same parameter. The layout is fixed
+when the material is built, and does not change the results: the
+computations are the same, only the addresses of the values change.
+
+A material stored component by component requires the integration by
+batches and the computations of the gradients, of the inner forces and of
+the stiffness matrices by kernels (or the tangent operator applied without
+assembly), which read the arrays through their strides. The integration
+point by point and the computations element by element read the values of
+a point as contiguous: they are refused at the setup of the problem (see
+below), and the methods of the behaviour integrators computing an element
+(:code:`integrate`, :code:`computeGradients`, :code:`computeInnerForces`,
+:code:`updateResidual`, :code:`updateJacobian`) throw an exception for
+such a material, so that a direct call can't give wrong values. For the
+same reason, the linearized operators (:code:`getLinearizedOperators`) and
+the resultant force on a boundary (:code:`computeResultantForceOnBoundary`),
+computed element by element, refuse such a material. The accessors of the
+material based on a stride between points (:code:`getGradient`,
+:code:`getThermodynamicForce`, :code:`getInternalStateVariable`...) refuse
+this layout, and an external state variable with several components
+computed by an evaluator can't be given to such a material. The arrays of
+the material (members :code:`s0`, :code:`s1` and :code:`K` of the material
+data manager of :code:`MGIS`) are stored in its layout: a code reading them
+directly must use the views of :code:`MGIS`, which account for the layout
+(:code:`getGradientsView`, :code:`getThermodynamicForcesView`,
+:code:`getInternalStateVariableView`, :code:`getTangentOperatorBlocksView`...).
+
 Consistency checks
 ------------------
 
